==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|wërden}}, from {{inh|de|goh|werdan}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*werþan}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*werþaną}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|worden}}, obsolete {{cog|en|worth}}, {{cog|sv|varda}}, {{cog|nn|verta}}, and also with {{cog|la|vertō||to turn}}.

The use as a passive auxiliary is old and found throughout West Germanic,<!-- incl. ME "worthen" --> whereas the use as a future auxiliary is a Middle High German innovation. It originated in [[inchoative]] constructions with the present participle: {{m|de||er wirt lachende|t=he starts laughing, is about to laugh, will laugh}}. Since the 14th century, the participle was increasingly replaced with the infinitive, probably by analogy with the older future auxiliaries {{m|de|wollen|t=will}} and {{m|de|sollen|t=shall}}. These latter were displaced by {{m|de||werden}} in Modern German, but survive dialectally.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈveːʁdən/|[ˈveːɐ̯.dn̩]|[ˈvɛɐ̯-]|[ʋ-]|[-dən]}}
* {{audio|de|De-werden.ogg}}
* {{audio|de|De-werden3.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|<irreg.sein>}}

# {{lb|de|auxiliary|past participle {{m|de|geworden}}}} [[will]]; to be [[going to]]; {{n-g|forms the future tense}} {{+obj|de|bare&inf<do something>}}
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''werde''' nach Hause gehen.|I '''will''' go home.}}
# {{lb|de|auxiliary|in the subjunctive}} [[would]]; {{n-g|forms the subjunctive tense of most verbs}} {{+obj|de|bare&inf<do something>}}
# {{lb|de|auxiliary|past participle {{m|de|worden}}}} to be done; {{n-g|forms the passive voice}} {{+obj|de|past&part}}
#: {{ux|de|Das Buch '''wird''' gerade gelesen.|q=present tense|The book '''is''' being read.}}
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''wurde''' in Europa geboren.|q=preterite tense|I '''was''' born in Europe.}}
#: {{ux|de|Er war geschlagen '''worden'''.|q=past perfect tense|He had '''been''' beaten.}}
# {{lb|de|copulative|past participle {{m|de|geworden}}}} to [[become]]; to [[get]]; to [[grow]]; to [[turn]]
#: {{ux|de|Es '''wird''' heißer.|It's '''getting''' hotter.}}
# for one to begin or come to [[feel]] or [[experience]] {{+obj|de|dat<for someone> + predicate&adjective<a certain state>}}
#: '''Usage:''' In this sense '''werden''' is always conjugated in the third person singular and takes a dative noun. The impersonal subject '''es''' may be present, but is often taken as implied. (See the usage note for a similar meaning of {{m|de|sein}}.)
#: {{uxi|de|Wird dir kalt?|Are you getting cold?}}
#: {{uxi|de|Den Kindern wird langweilig.|The children are getting bored.}}
#: {{ux|de|Von Mayonnaise wird mir schlecht.|Mayonnaise makes me sick.|lit=From mayonnaise I become sick.}}
# {{lb|de|copulative|colloquial}} to [[be]]; to [[happen]]; to [[occur]] {{q|in the future}}
#: {{ux|de|Wir '''werden''' zusammen glücklich.|We ''will be'' happy together.}}
#: {{ux|de|Was wird aus mir?|What will become of me?}}
# {{lb|de|colloquial}} to be acceptable; to function correctly; to have the desired result or effect
#: {{ux|de|Das '''wird''' so nichts.|It '''will not work''' like that.
}}
#: {{syn|de|klappen|funktionieren}}

