==Middle Low German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|gml|osx|wērthan||to become}}, from {{inh|gml|gmw-pro|*werþan}}, from {{inh|gml|gem-pro|*werþaną}}.

===Pronunciation===
* '''[[Wiktionary:About_Middle_Low_German#Stem_vowels|Stem vowel]]: ê²'''
** {{IPA|gml|/wɛːrdən/|a=originally}} or {{IPA|gml|/wærdən/}}
** <small>While the combination /rd/ originally lengthened the vowel in Old Saxon, in several Middle Low German dialects it was treated like a [[geminate#Noun|geminate]], or had actually become /r/, and in turn shortened long vowels occurring before it. Further, the vowel was shortened before /rt/ from [[final obstruent devoicing]]. Dialects then often begun to apply the more common vowel length across all forms. </small>

